+# Benchmark record
+
+Exactly 15 benchmark invocations are permitted. Logs are in results/NN.log.
+
+| Run | Changes | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Original Go application | PASS 3,673 |
+| 2 | Indexes, aggregate statistics, set moderation, pool and MySQL tuning | PASS 22,002 |
+| 3 | Icon hashes/304, per-request response caches, tag joins, DNS name index | PASS 43,549 |
+| 4 | Shared metadata caches, direct transactional DNS registration, DNS TTL/cache/logging | PASS 69,009 |
+| 5 | API load balancing across s2/s3, 750ms icon cache, upstream keepalive | PASS 188,766 |
+| 6 | Frontend/TLS moved to s2, database and DNS on s1 | PASS 238,026 |
+| 7 | Indexed ranking counters maintained transactionally by triggers | PASS 270,845 |
+| 8 | Autocommit ordinary reads and covering tip/emoji indexes | PASS 271,524 |
+| 9 | Binary prepared icon inserts, Go SHA256, binary logging disabled | PASS 247,858 |
+| 10 | User domains split across s2 and s3 TLS frontends | PASS 273,322 |
+| 11 | Immutable user metadata reuse, batch tag search, larger redo log and I/O capacity | PASS 294,266 |
+| 12 | Balance initial DNS names, gzip JSON at level 1 | PASS 274,967 |
+| 13 | Icon proxy cache, pool 16, logs reduced, full reboot and validation | PASS 301,968 |
+| 14 | Stable DNS zone caches, second full reboot validation | PASS 291,157 |
+| 15 | Final: run 13 application and DNS settings; reboot delay fixed | See results/15.log |
+
+Server private IPs: s1=10.0.1.229, s2=10.0.1.47, s3=10.0.1.135.
diff --git a/ops/README.md b/ops/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ca66d1a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ops/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Deployment and operation
+
+Roles: s1 holds primary MySQL and authoritative PowerDNS; s2 and s3 run identical Go apps and HTTPS frontends. All applications use s1's MySQL. s1 also runs the app to handle initialization. Nginx on both frontends directs `/api/initialize` to s1. Initialization clears local and peer response caches.
+
+All services use enabled systemd units. Application environments are `/home/isucon/env.sh`. `ISUPIPE_APP_ADDRESS` and `ISUPIPE_SECONDARY_APP_ADDRESS` keep DNS destinations stable independently of the original boot helper.
+
+`deploy-binary.sh /absolute/path/to/binary` updates the three installed app executables. Build with `/home/isucon/local/golang/bin/go build` on a server in `/home/isucon/webapp/go`.
+
+Schema changes were applied sequentially: `webapp/sql/tune.sql`, `icons.sql`, `scores.sql`, `covering.sql`, `icons_plain.sql`. Ranking triggers and tables persist in MySQL. The modified `init.sql` truncates the ranking tables before loading initial data; insert triggers rebuild them.
+
+PowerDNS records have an index on `(name,type)`. Registration inserts its DNS record in the same database transaction as the user. Valid user domains are divided between both frontends. DNS negative caching stays disabled to keep new registrations visible.
+
+User icons and hashes expire in the app cache after 250ms for image bytes and 750ms for user API hashes; writes invalidate the local cache. Nginx icon responses expire at the end of the current clock second through an absolute X-Accel-Expires header, bounding combined staleness below two seconds. Immutable stream metadata and user profile fields are reused. `check-icon-freshness.py` verifies the two-server freshness and conditional GET behavior.
+
+Benchmark logs and the exact run count are recorded in `RESULTS.md` and `results/NN.log`. Do not invoke `bench` after run 15.
+
+The final app pool has 16 connections per process. The positive DNS query cache uses 60s; zone and metadata caches are disabled after the run 14 comparison. DNS caches are purged on initialization. The OS motd-news service and timer are masked to avoid their observed 90s shutdown timeout. Full three-server reboot checks are recorded in results/reboot*.log.
+
+Final selection uses the run 13 application binary and DNS settings (301,968 points), retaining the shutdown fix. Run 14 also passed after a second full reboot (291,157 points). JSON compression is disabled. Run 15 is the final benchmark and its output is in results/15.log.
diff --git a/ops/check-icon-freshness.py b/ops/check-icon-freshness.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8e36b8e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ops/check-icon-freshness.py
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+import hashlib,json,time,urllib.request,urllib.error,http.cookies,ssl
+from pathlib import Path
+opener=urllib.request.build_opener(urllib.request.ProxyHandler({}),urllib.request.HTTPSHandler(context=ssl._create_unverified_context()))
+cookie=''
+def req(addr,path,body=None,etag=None):
+ headers={'Host':'pipe.u.isucon.dev','Cookie':cookie}
+ if body is not None:headers['Content-Type']='application/json'
+ if etag is not None:headers['If-None-Match']='"'+etag+'"'
+ request=urllib.request.Request('https://'+addr+path,data=body,headers=headers)
+ try:r=opener.open(request,timeout=5)
+ except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:r=e
+ with r:return r.code,dict(r.headers),r.read()
+status,headers,body=req('127.0.0.1','/api/login',b'{"username":"test001","password":"test"}')
+assert status==200,(status,body)
+jar=http.cookies.SimpleCookie();jar.load(headers['Set-Cookie']);cookie='SESSIONID='+jar['SESSIONID'].value
+addrs=['10.0.1.47','10.0.1.135']
+old=[]
+for addr in addrs:
+ status,_,body=req(addr,'/api/user/test001');assert status==200
+ old.append(json.loads(body)['icon_hash'])
+ status,_,_=req(addr,'/api/user/test001/icon');assert status==200
+image=Path('/home/isucon/webapp/img/NoImage.jpg').read_bytes()+b'\nicon freshness check '+str(time.time_ns()).encode()+b'\n'
+import base64
+expected=hashlib.sha256(image).hexdigest();started=time.monotonic()
+status,_,body=req(addrs[0],'/api/icon',json.dumps({'image':base64.b64encode(image).decode()}).encode());assert status==201,(status,body)
+time.sleep(1.55)
+for addr,previous in zip(addrs,old):
+ status,_,body=req(addr,'/api/user/test001');assert status==200
+ assert json.loads(body)['icon_hash']==expected,(addr,'stale API hash')
+ status,_,body=req(addr,'/api/user/test001/icon',etag=previous)
+ assert status==200 and hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest()==expected,(addr,'stale conditional image',status,hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest(),expected)
+ status,_,body=req(addr,'/api/user/test001/icon',etag=expected);assert status==304,(addr,status)
+ status,_,body=req(addr,'/api/user/test001/icon');assert status==200 and hashlib.sha256(body).hexdigest()==expected
+elapsed=time.monotonic()-started
+assert elapsed<2,elapsed
+print('PASS: icon API hashes, new bytes, conditional 304 and unconditional 200 on both app servers after %.3fs'%elapsed)
